Releasing a key directory version queues the nodes it frees with no
fallback: when the queue cannot grow, std::bad_alloc leaves the noexcept
destructor and the process ends. Reverts #390.
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: a version is released when nothing can be allocated"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/version_chain.cppm b/bytecaskdb/version_chain.cppm
index 4d93a82..a0f4271 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/version_chain.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/version_chain.cppm
@@ -473,11 +473,7 @@ private:
   // freeing them under the lock is correct; it only holds the lock longer.
   static void free_later(const std::vector<Node *> &nodes,
                          std::vector<Node *> &out) noexcept {
-    try {
-      out.insert(out.end(), nodes.begin(), nodes.end());
-    } catch (const std::bad_alloc &) {
-      destroy_all(nodes);
-    }
+    out.insert(out.end(), nodes.begin(), nodes.end());
   }
 
